Frequency list
  https://github.com/hermitdave/FrequencyWords
  content/2018/en/en_50k.txt
  Content licence: Creative Commons Attribution-ShareAlike 4.0 International
  https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/
  Built from the OpenSubtitles 2018 corpus. Used for the common-word flag and
  the five frequency bars. Rank 1 is the most frequent word in that list.
  Bars: 1-1000 = 5, 1001-3000 = 4, 3001-8000 = 3, 8001-20000 = 2,
  20001-50000 = 1. Words in the top 20,000 are marked common.

Fonts
  Literata (OFL 1.1) and Source Sans 3 (OFL 1.1), shipped as WOFF2 for the
  pages. https://github.com/googlefonts/literata
  https://github.com/adobe-fonts/source-sans

Merge order used by tools/import.php
  Wiktionary (Kaikki) first, then Open English WordNet, then Moby Thesaurus.
  WordNet does not replace a Wiktionary sense. It adds a part of speech only
  when Wiktionary has none for that part of speech, and it adds synonym,
  antonym, hypernym, and related links. Moby adds extra synonyms only.
  Tatoeba fills an example only when a sense has none. CMUdict fills IPA only
  when an entry has none. Every stored row keeps its source name.
